        "original_id": "b84763bb-53b4-5a53-82c6-d461f22ec063",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lesquerella, Thujopsis, Paysonia, Physaria\n- Plant families: Cupressaceae\n- Chemicals: Lesquerolic acid\n- Concepts: flowering plant genera, conifers, genetic and morphological classification\n\nFacts:\n- Lesquerella is the former name of a genus of flowering plants.\n- Thujopsis is a conifer in the cypress family Cupressaceae, and Thujopsis dolabrata is the only member of the genus Thujopsis.\n- Until 2002, Paysonia was considered part of the genus Lesquerella, but Paysonia was separated based on genetic and morphological features.\n- Lesquerolic acid is a hydroxy acid that occurs naturally in Paysonia lasiocarpa and in other Paysonia and Physaria species.",
